Roll the library-engine pin forward, and say why nothing rolled it

## What this does

Moves `.library-engine` from `61613f6` to `8ede250`, its engine's current `main` —
22 commits. The old pin was a strict ancestor, so this is a fast-forward; there is
no divergence to resolve and nothing to reconcile.

## The finding, which matters more than the bump

**The library engine is the only mounted engine that nothing rolls forward.**

`modules-upgrade.yml` runs four jobs — journal, atlas, tell, antidote — and each one
`uses:` that module's *own* `.github/actions/advance-engine`. I checked all five
mounts:

| engine | ships `advance-engine`? | rolled by a job? |
|---|---|---|
| journal | yes | yes |
| atlas | yes | yes |
| tell | yes | yes |
| antidote | yes | yes |
| **library** | **no** | **no** |

That is consistent rather than an oversight in isolation: `AGENTS.md` notes the
library engine ships no build, and `advance-engine`'s whole job is to build-gate a
candidate pin before writing it back. No build → no action → no job.

But the consequence was not chosen: this pin cannot move on its own, so it will
drift again by exactly this much, silently, and the next person will bump it by
hand again. `modules-force-pin.yml` is not a fallback either — its `module` choice
list is `journal`/`atlas`/`tell` only, so the one engine with no scheduled roller
is also the one the manual escape hatch cannot name.

## What was verified, and how

- Pins read from the tree (`git ls-tree origin/main <path>`), not from the
  checkout, per `AGENTS.md`. All six recorded pins matched their checkouts on a
  fresh thaw — no `+` in `git submodule status`, so nothing had drifted locally.
- The other five pins are already at their engine's `origin/main`. Only the
  library engine was behind.
- `git merge-base --is-ancestor 61613f6 origin/main` → true (fast-forward).
- The 22 commits touch `ADOPTING.md`, `GRANTS.md`, `OPEN.md`, `README.md`,
  `adoption/README.md`, `adoption/engines.yml`, `adoption/worked/artist-lockers.md`
  — documentation and adoption config, no build output. There is nothing here a
  build gate would have caught, which is why bumping it ungated is safe *this time*
  and is not an argument that it is safe in general.
- Staged by name (`git add -- .library-engine`), pin only. `git diff --cached
  --stat` shows one file, one line.

## Deliberately not done

- **No roller job added here.** Adding a `library` job to `modules-upgrade.yml`
  would reference `./.library-engine/.github/actions/advance-engine`, which does not
  exist — the fix has to start in the library engine, a repo this one does not own.
  That is a petition, not a commit in this PR, and it is not filed yet.
- **Not added to `modules-force-pin.yml`'s choice list.** That would be a real
  one-line improvement and needs no upstream change, but it is a different concern
  from this bump and belongs in its own PR so you can take one and sit on the other.
  Worth noting `all` there expands to `journal atlas tell`, so it misses antidote
  too.

## The decision for you

Whether the library engine should grow a build-less `advance-engine` (one that
rolls without gating, since there is no build to gate), or whether this pin is
meant to be moved by hand as an editorial act. Both are defensible. Right now it is
neither — it is unrolled by accident and looks identical to healthy.
